# A three-word review can stop the work.

> **“This is wrong.”**

<!-- Picture this. You open a pull request and see a comment: “This is wrong.” -->

---

# Clear feedback replaces guessing with a next step.

## Risk → Reason → Route

<!-- The receiver gets a risk, a reason and a route forward. -->

---

# Useful feedback is specific and human.

## Notice → Effect → Next step

<!-- Say what you noticed. Explain the effect. Invite the next step. -->

---

# Feedback improves when you practise the next sentence.

## “Thoughts?” → “Where could this fail?”

<!-- When you ask for feedback, replace “Thoughts?” with a target. -->

---

# Clear concerns turn reviews into shared debugging.

## You vs me ↓ Us vs problem

<!-- Not you versus me, but both of us versus the problem. -->

